---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

// The policy text is held inline here, deliberately, rather than in a content
// collection. Collections run text through frontmatter and Markdown processing,
// which is where a quote or a dash quietly changes. This is a legal notice
// published to Google as Stewardmark's binding policy: it ships exactly as
// written, or not at all.
const title = 'Privacy Notice | Stewardmark';
const description =
  'How Stewardmark, LLC handles information collected through this website and our client portal.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="band legal">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <h1 class="legal__title">Privacy Notice</h1>
      <p class="legal__effective">Effective September 11, 2026</p>

      <p>
        This notice describes how Stewardmark, LLC ("Stewardmark," "we," "us"), a
        California limited liability company based in Berkeley, California, handles
        information collected through this website and our client portal.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Website analytics.</strong> We use basic analytics to understand how
        visitors use this site, such as pages viewed and general location. We do not
        use advertising pixels or sell visitor data.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Client portal sign-in.</strong> Access to our client portal is
        protected by Cloudflare Access. When you sign in with your Google or other
        identity provider account, we receive your name and email address so we can
        verify who you are. We do not receive your password.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Client intake and engagement information.</strong> When you complete
        our intake form or work with us, we collect the information you choose to
        provide, such as your name, contact details, organization, and information
        about your project or matter.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        We use a small number of cookies and similar technologies to operate the
        site and to understand which pages people read. We do not use advertising
        cookies or advertising pixels, and we do not permit third parties to use
        this site to build advertising profiles. Our analytics provider may set a
        cookie to distinguish one visit from another. You can block or delete
        cookies in your browser; the site works without them.
      </p>

      <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
      <p>
        Some browsers send a Do Not Track signal. There is no common industry
        standard for how to interpret it. We do not track visitors across other
        websites or over time for advertising, so our behavior does not change
        based on the signal. We do not permit third parties to collect personally
        identifiable information about our visitors across other sites.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use this information to provide and manage our consulting services,
        respond to inquiries, secure the client portal, and meet our legal and
        professional obligations. We do not sell personal information, and we do not
        share it with third parties for their own marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>Phone numbers and text messaging</h2>
      <p>
        If you provide a mobile number, we may contact you by text about your
        engagement. Mobile information will not be shared with third parties or
        affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. We do not share or sell
        consumer personal information, including phone numbers and SMS consent, to
        third parties or affiliates for marketing or lead generation purposes. All
        other categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent;
        this information will not be shared with any third parties. Message and data
        rates may apply.
        Message frequency varies. Reply STOP to opt out, HELP for help.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on a small number of service providers to operate this site and our
        business, including Cloudflare (website hosting and portal security), Google
        (identity sign-in and business email), and similar infrastructure providers.
        They process information on our behalf to deliver those services.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        We keep client information for as long as needed to serve the engagement and
        to satisfy legal, professional, and recordkeeping obligations, then dispose
        of it. We use reasonable safeguards to protect information, including
        encryption in transit and multi-factor authentication on the systems we
        control. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may contact us at any time to ask what information we hold about you, to
        request a correction, or to request deletion, subject to our legal and
        professional retention obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>If you are a California resident</h2>
      <p>
        Stewardmark is below the thresholds that make the California Consumer
        Privacy Act apply to us. We honor its core requests regardless. Write to{' '}
        <Fragment set:html={'<!--email_off-->'} /><a href="mailto:privacy@stewardmark.ai"
          >privacy@stewardmark.ai</a
        ><Fragment set:html={'<!--/email_off-->'} /> and you may ask what personal
        information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete
        it. We do not sell or share personal information, so there is nothing to
        opt out of. We will not treat you differently for making a request.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed to children under 13 and we do not knowingly
        collect their personal information. If you believe a child has provided us
        information, write to{' '}
        <Fragment set:html={'<!--email_off-->'} /><a href="mailto:privacy@stewardmark.ai"
          >privacy@stewardmark.ai</a
        ><Fragment set:html={'<!--/email_off-->'} /> and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this notice can be sent to{' '}
        <Fragment set:html={'<!--email_off-->'} /><a href="mailto:privacy@stewardmark.ai"
          >privacy@stewardmark.ai</a
        ><Fragment set:html={'<!--/email_off-->'} />.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We review this notice at least once a year, and whenever we change the
        systems or services that handle personal information. If we change it, we
        post the updated version here with a new effective date. This notice was
        last reviewed on September 11, 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: var(--section-pad-y) 0;
  }
  .legal__inner {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }
  .legal__title {
    font-size: var(--text-h2-size);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .legal__effective {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    /* Same colour as the headings. The band sets --text-on-dark; anything from
       the light-surface palette (--text-body) is near-black on this background. */
    color: var(--text-on-dark);
    margin: 8px 0 32px;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 36px 0 10px;
  }
  .legal p {
    font-size: var(--text-body-size);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--text-on-dark);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
  .legal a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
</style>
